              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Bonnie I. Robin-Vergeer, remon Lee is serving a life sentence without possibility of parole for first\u2011degree murder and argues he never had a chance to present testimony from witnesses who could have established his innocence."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Bonnie I. Robin-Vergeer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "03f04d4408c6652bcf5c65375827cdc22ea9a89875c425f4babd5c6a425e2f99",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-03f04d4408c6-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Bonnie I. Robin-Vergeer, lee contends that his failure to comply with two Missouri rules governing motions for continuance should not be an adequate State\u2011law ground to bar consideration of his federal due\u2011process claim."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Defendant",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "03f04d4408c6652bcf5c65375827cdc22ea9a89875c425f4babd5c6a425e2f99",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-03f04d4408c6-0003-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 57,
              "start": 57
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Defendant, lee alleges that the trial court denied his rights to due process of law and to effective assistance of counsel guaranteed by the Sixth and Fourteenth Amendments when it overruled his motion for a continuance."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court Record",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "03f04d4408c6652bcf5c65375827cdc22ea9a89875c425f4babd5c6a425e2f99",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-03f04d4408c6-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 49,
              "start": 49
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "A new\u2011trial motion was filed two weeks after trial and was not heard until two months after trial."
      }
    ],
